
What is Traversal?

Traversal means:

Visit every element of the array exactly once.

Think of standing in front of a line of people. To know everyone's name, you simply walk from the first person to the last. That's traversal.
Array

5 3 7 2 9

↓

5 → 3 → 7 → 2 → 9

Universal Formula

Whenever a question says:

Find...
Count...
Print...
Check...
Update...
Search...

your first thought should be:

"Can I solve this by looking at each element once?"

If yes, use traversal.

Universal Traversal Template (Java)
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

    // Process current element

}
or
for (int num : arr) {

    // Process current element

}

Revision Notes (1-Minute Recall)
Visit each element once.
Best for counting, searching, summing, printing, checking.
Usually one for loop.
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
Think: "Can I solve this in one pass?"


